findings:
- finding_id: C1
  title: from_file_or_default swallows ALL errors including parse and permission failures
  weight: 8
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase addressed from_file_or_default swallowing all errors. The config
    implementation uses from_file() and from_file_with_env() but no evidence of distinguishing
    NotFound from parse/permission errors. The TEA tests and reviewer comments don't
    flag this specific issue.
- finding_id: I1
  title: CliError Display leaks internal details to stderr (CWE-209)
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: dev
  evidence: "Reviewer verified: 'CWE-209 error sanitization \u2014 Display impls are\
    \ generic, internal details hidden at error.rs:10-42'. Dev implemented sanitized\
    \ Display. However, the stderr eprintln! path was not explicitly flagged \u2014\
    \ the Display impl itself is sanitized but the reviewer didn't flag that eprintln!\
    \ still prints Display directly. Partial catch by dev implementing sanitized Display."
- finding_id: I2
  title: "SiemClient.tenant_id uses raw String \u2014 header injection risk (CWE-113)"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: SiemClient.tenant_id uses raw String. TEA wrote header injection tests
    for CRLF/null bytes, and dev implemented CRLF validation, but neither phase flagged
    that tenant_id should use the validated TenantId type from axiathon-core instead
    of raw String. The CRLF check is a band-aid; the type-safety issue (bypassing
    TenantId) was not caught.
- finding_id: I3
  title: Dependencies use direct version strings instead of workspace = true
  weight: 3
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: "Dev added 6 dependencies (clap_complete, comfy-table, csv, dirs, reqwest,\
    \ toml) to workspace dependencies but the reviewer noted a toml version mismatch\
    \ \u2014 no phase flagged that crate Cargo.toml uses direct version strings instead\
    \ of workspace = true references."
- finding_id: I4
  title: "Config token field silently ignored \u2014 secret left on disk"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: 'Reviewer flagged as [HIGH]: ''RawConfig silently ignores unknown fields
    at config.rs:10-15... A user who puts token = "secret" in their config file gets
    zero feedback... Should fix: Add #[serde(deny_unknown_fields)] to RawConfig.'''
- finding_id: I5
  title: "Vacuously true test \u2014 assertion is None || true"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified the vacuously true assertion pattern (is_none() ||
    ...). The reviewer noted the security test at security.rs:88-110 'has an empty
    body' in an if-let branch but did not specifically flag the None || true tautology
    in config tests.
- finding_id: I6
  title: "Test with zero assertions \u2014 only checks non-panic"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase flagged the zero-assertion test that only checks non-panic with
    'let _ = config'. TEA wrote config tests but did not identify this specific pattern
    in the test suite.
